// --raw-pointer-audit publishes one GTI-S2102 for an unsafe access observed
// both directly and through its checked owner (reproducer A44), as a warning
// under warn and an error under strict, nothing when off, and a separate
// finding for each distinct access with the same origin. (From
// testRawAuditDiagnosticPublication in compiler_diagnostics_tests.cpp.)
$ gti one_access.gti --emit-mir -o out.mir --raw-pointer-audit=warn
stderr: $DIR/one_access.gti:15:42: warning[GTI-S2102]
stderr: $DIR/one_access.gti:12:26: note: Raw address obtained here.
stdout: Diagnostics: 0 errors, 1 warning
$ gti one_access.gti --emit-mir -o out.mir --raw-pointer-audit=strict
? 65
stderr: $DIR/one_access.gti:15:42: error[GTI-S2102]
stdout: Diagnostics: 1 error, 0 warnings
$ gti one_access.gti --emit-mir -o out.mir
stdout: Diagnostics: 0 errors, 0 warnings
$ gti two_accesses.gti --emit-mir -o out.mir --raw-pointer-audit=warn
stderr: $DIR/two_accesses.gti:15:42: warning[GTI-S2102]
stderr: $DIR/two_accesses.gti:16:47: warning[GTI-S2102]
stdout: Diagnostics: 0 errors, 2 warnings
